#test "service metadata preserves exact byte ceilings and rejects independent invalid facts" {
 text:[1025]u8;for i:0..<text.count {text[i]='x';}i:=[1]CtInfo.[CtInfo.{operation="x",model="m",provider="p",revision=1}];
 #assert ctr_info_valid(i[..]);
 for field:0..<7 {
  limit:=ifx field==0 || field==2 || field==4 then 80 else ifx field==1 then 160 else ifx field==3 then 16 else 1024;
  for extra:0..<2 {s:=cast(string)text[0..<limit+extra];
   if field==0 {i[0].operation=s;}if field==1 {i[0].model=s;}if field==2 {i[0].provider=s;}if field==3 {i[0].effort=s;}if field==4 {i[0].route=s;}if field==5 {i[0].why=s;}if field==6 {i[0].why=s;}
   #assert ctr_info_valid(i[..])==(extra==0);
  }
  i[0]=CtInfo.{operation="x",model="m",provider="p",revision=1};
 }
 v:[1]CtView;b:[8192]u8;_=ct_view_begin(v[..],CT_TEST_CONVERSATION,CT_TEST_TURN);
 i[0].operation="";#assert ctr_turn_write(v[..],i[..],b[..])<0;i[0].operation="x";v[0].state=0;#assert ctr_turn_write(v[..],i[..],b[..])<0;v[0].state=CT_QUEUED;
 n:=ctr_turn_write(v[..],i[..],b[..]);d:[1]Jv;nodes:[64]JvNode;#assert n>0 && jv_parse(d[..],cast(string)b[0..<n],nodes[..]) && jv_len(d[0],jv_get(d[0],0,"content"))==0;
 ct_record_running(v[..]);v[0].bytes=1;n=ctr_turn_write(v[..],i[..],b[..]);#assert n>0 && jv_parse(d[..],cast(string)b[0..<n],nodes[..]) && jv_len(d[0],jv_get(d[0],0,"content"))==1;
 n=ctr_answer_message(v[..],0,b[..]);#assert n>0 && jv_parse(d[..],cast(string)b[0..<n],nodes[..]);at:=jv_at(d[0],jv_get(d[0],0,"content"),0);#assert jv_raw(d[0],jv_get(d[0],at,"text"))=="H";
}
// Three full escaped writes plus the independent decode exceed 100M evaluator
// steps; the native check and mutation baseline exercise the same full ceiling.
#test "full replies validate every byte without a hidden 64KiB limit" #steps 200000000 {
 v:[1]CtView;ct_record_running(v[..]);v[0].sequence=CT_SEQUENCE_MAX;v[0].bytes=131072;for j:0..<v[0].bytes {v[0].content[j]='x';}#assert ctr_view_valid(v[..]);
 // Every byte needs a six-byte JSON escape. Test the actual writer, its
 // decoded content and its exact encoded capacity, not only a view validator.
 for j:0..<v[0].bytes {v[0].content[j]=1;}out:[1048576]u8;i:=[1]CtInfo.[CtInfo.{operation="x",model="m",provider="p",revision=1}];
 n:=ctr_turn_write(v[..],i[..],out[..]);#assert n>786432 && n<1048576;d:[1]Jv;nodes:[64]JvNode;#assert jv_parse(d[..],cast(string)out[0..<n],nodes[..]);at:=jv_at(d[0],jv_get(d[0],0,"content"),0);decoded:[131072]u8;#assert js_string(d[0],jv_get(d[0],at,"text"),decoded[..])==131072 && decoded[0]==1 && decoded[131071]==1;
 #assert ctr_turn_write(v[..],i[..],out[0..<n-1])<0 && ctr_turn_write(v[..],i[..],out[0..<n])==n;
 v[0].state=CT_FAILED;v[0].nr=js_copy(v[0].reason[..],"error");v[0].ne=512;for j:0..<512 {v[0].error[j]='e';}#assert ctr_view_valid(v[..]);
 v[0].bytes=0;v[0].error[511]=255;#assert !ctr_view_valid(v[..]);
}
